    {
      "id": "on592lm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.2 Forest Cover"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Van Panchayats and Conservation",
      "id": "gr59o0n"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t2ogrlj",
      "content": "About 71% of Uttarakhand's area is forested — among the highest proportions in India. Forest types range from tropical moist deciduous in the Terai to subalpine conifer and alpine meadows (Bugiyal) at high altitudes. The state has significant Van Panchayat (community forest councils) — over 12,000 Van Panchayats manage community forests."
    },
