    {
      "id": "azcd1rv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.5 Van Panchayats and Conservation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ykxd13v",
      "content": "Uttarakhand has over 12,000 Van Panchayats (community forest councils), which manage about 5 lakh hectares of 'community forests'. This institution dates back to 1931 (UP Panchayat Forest Rules). Van Panchayats have played a crucial role in forest conservation and are considered a model of community-based management."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w048yap",
      "content": "Chipko Movement: Born in Uttarakhand (1973–74). Villagers of Reni village (Chamoli) — led by Gaura Devi and Chandi Prasad Bhatt — hugged trees to prevent commercial felling. The movement spread globally as an environmental protest symbol. Sundarlal Bahuguna was a key organizer. 'Chipko' means 'to stick/hug'."
    },
